      "id": "69a49888308c21b804c7",
      "name": "azove",
      "epoch": "0",
      "version": "2.0",
      "release": "33.fc44",
      "architecture": "amd64",
      "summary": "Another Zero-One Vertex Enumeration tool",
      "description": "Azove is a tool designed for counting (without explicit enumeration) and\nenumeration of 0/1 vertices.  Given a polytope by a linear relaxation or facet\ndescription `P = {x | Ax <= b}`, all 0/1 points lying in P can be counted or\nenumerated.  This is done by intersecting the polytope P with the\nunit-hypercube `[0,1] d`.  The integral vertices (no fractional ones) of this\nintersection will be enumerated.  If P is a 0/1 polytope, azove solves the\nvertex enumeration problem.  In fact it can also solve the 0/1 knapsack\nproblem and the 0/1 subset sum problem.",
      "homepage": "https://people.mpi-inf.mpg.de/alumni/d1/2019/behle/azove.html",
